-- KB rules, transcribed from the KB sheet (kb_id, topic, guidance only). Edit in the Supabase Table Editor.
-- Round 1 additions (edge cases). Proposed by Claude; review and edit in the Table Editor.
('KB-18','Delayed settlement past expected date','If a settlement marked ''Delayed'' has passed its expected settlement date, or has no expected date, do not share the old date or any new date. Acknowledge the delay and confirm the case has been escalated to the settlements team for priority review. Merchants can track status on Dashboard > Settlements.'),
('KB-19','Settlement amount different from expected','If a merchant says a settlement amount is lower or different than expected, do not explain deductions, fees, refunds or adjustments that are not shown in the system, and do not say whether the amount is correct. Point them to Dashboard > Settlements and escalate the query to the Account Manager for reconciliation.'),
('KB-20','GST invoice not available','If a GST invoice is not visible, remind the merchant that invoices are generated by the 5th of every month under Dashboard > Reports > Invoices. If it is still missing after that, escalate to the Account Manager. Do not promise a date for a missing invoice.'),
('KB-21','Enterprise merchants','Every reply to an Enterprise merchant is reviewed by a support agent before it is sent, and the merchant''s Account Manager is kept informed of any escalation. Do not commit to anything on the Account Manager''s behalf.'),
('KB-22','Requests from a merchant''s customers','If the person writing is a customer of a merchant rather than the merchant, do not share any merchant account, settlement or business details, and do not confirm or deny any specific payment. Share only general guidance on failed payments and refunds, and advise them to contact the merchant, or their bank with the payment reference, for order-specific help.'),
('KB-23','Sensitive data shared in a message','If a message contains an OTP, password, PIN, CVV, full card number, Aadhaar number or full bank account number, never repeat it in the reply. Remind the sender not to share these details over email or chat; the support team will never ask for them.'),
('KB-24','Documents sent to support','KYC and verification documents are accepted only through Dashboard > Account > KYC. Support cannot accept documents sent by email or attached to a ticket. Ask the merchant to upload them on the Dashboard.'),
('KB-25','Language not supported','Replies are written in English or Hinglish. If the merchant writes in another language, reply in simple English, and an agent reviews the reply before it is sent.'),
('KB-26','KYC hold pending for a long time','If a settlement has been held for KYC for longer than expected, an agent checks the KYC submission before replying. Guide the merchant to Dashboard > Account > KYC to confirm all documents are uploaded, and do not promise a release date.')
on conflict (kb_id) do nothing;
